I've been playing nethack for about 4 years now, off and on.  Been
"off" for over a year, but something lately got me thinking about it...
 A full moon?  I picked it back up, and boy did I pass a milestone!

Early in the game I found some killer items: a magic whistle, a (+0)
Helm of Brilliance, +5 elven mithril, and I knew this would be a very
special game.  I made it to the bottom of the mines to find a Minotaur.
 Run away!  But I came back later, invisible and stealthy and armed
with some mean wands, and killed him.  I #dipped and got Excalibur,
then I searched for the polytrap that I knew had to be there.  I found
my very first polytrap--at least, the first one I'd found some way
other than stepping on it.  I leashed my cat, dragged him across, and
on my first ever polypet attempt got Felix the arch-lich. ohohohoho.  I
looted the gems, tripe-tamed a dog on the way out and turned him into
Ruff the Umber Hulk.  I'd never before seen an arch-lich or umber hulk
in game, but they looked pretty formidable to me.

Proceeded to pet-cleanout pretty much any shop or temple that I wanted
to, including a spellbook shop in Minetown and a nice ring shop on dlvl
3.  I love watching these guys fight.  Felix is creepy with that
freezing touch, but Ruff is so cool, confusing things.  Found a nice
bones file with a corroded katana, burnt +4 mummy wrapping, robe and
nice scrolls.

Funny / interesting mental images:
- Too-cleverly trying to fix my corroded katana by letting Ruff confuse
me so I could read a ?oEA.  Not my smartest play of the game.
- Running back and forth on the Oracle level trying to get my pets to
kill a white unicorn so I could get the horn.  Umber hulk crushing
walls, generally reaking havoc, Oracle becoming collateral damage.
Gave up after a while. (and eventually found a black unicorn in
sokoban.)
- Solved 2 soko puzzles without cheating, but I had to strip on the
third one.  Killed a tiger naked, with my bare hands. **flex**
- Went back and Felix had gone peaceful.  At least he didn't go wild,
that probably would have been YASD for me.
- Ruff the umber hulk standing in the middle of the sokoban zoo,
confusing everything around.  Then getting killed.  I genuinely had a
sad feeling for that guy.
- Revisited the Mine's End polytrap to get a new uber-pet.  Got Zipper
the pit fiend, then accidentally stepped on the trap and turned into a
brown mold.  Split my b+5 mithril, Apply katana "." Ugh.

Noteworthy before Medusa:
- got 2 ?oG.  That's G for Genocide.
- got a +oID that with my +2HoB and robe I could cast at a very usable
67% fail hoo hooo grr stampa stampa
- no bigroom
- no Ludios, and I did look for it.
- first time ever for Rogue level or anything past that.
- When I met Surtur, I suddenly had the boss music from FFVI going
through my head.  He went down without a big scare and got the Orb of
heavy-but-too-good-to-bag Fate and the Bell of Opening, my first quest
artifact / invocation artifact ever.

I felt skiddish levitating across Medusa's swamp... never had a deadly
encounter with a ; before, and I didn't want to have my first here.
Didn't have anything slippery to wear.  Didn't have any swimming gear.
I did have these 2 blessed scrolls of G though. *sigh* sorry fish-kind.
 Got to the island, and in one of the outer chambers I met my first
mind-flayer. Hm, and I still had a b?oG. Sorry mind-flayer kind,
dwarf-kind, and hobbit-kind.  Didn't know what exactly to expect from
Medusa, besides a stoning gaze, so I meticulously towel-blinded myself,
stethescoped her, made sure I was reflective, twoweaponed Excalibur and
the katana, and chop-chopped.  Didn't kill her in one chop-chop, but
she woke up, looked at me, and statuefied in the same turn.  Kind of
anticlimactic.  Perseus just had a sack.  Bleh.

Opened the castle with a +oKnock that I found in the outside maze,
first time I cast it.  I really lucked out here because I wasn't aware
what a deathtrap the drawbridge can be or what a challenge it sometimes
is to get in there. =oConflict and some pets cleaned it out pretty much
for me, although Zipper got statued in the process.

Found the WoW in the first turret I checked.  I had such a nice kit, I
basically had wishes to burn, so I saved a few.  Also got another
couple b?oG, since the first were so handy. On the way out I had my
first ever encounter with a L.  Malignant aura?  After chop-chopping
him with my Excalibur and katana in a couple of turns, I decided that
random cursing was not something I wanted to deal with in the future.
Sorry L-kind (including *sniff* poor Felix back on Sokoban lev.2, who
done me nothin' but good)

-- side note: shouldn't there be an alignment / luck penalty for
genocide, especially for lawfuls, especially genociding pets, peaceful
monsters or even entire species of peaceful monsters? --

I converted the storerooms into my personal stash/fortress, then
outside of that store I lost my =oL in a blind Mojo-tossing incident.
Fortunately I had a huge sack of rings and wands named made redundant
that I'd left with Medusa because I didn't want to fall down the
stairs, and it had another =oL in it.

I went on down to Gehennom.  Fought Asmodeus.  He didn't die, but he
was nowhere to be found.  Huh.  Tamed a red dragon.  kept on exploring,
collected some scrolls and wands and decided to head back to the castle
and stash it.  On the way back up Asmodeus arrived again. He killed
Scorch in one blast of cold.  Finally I beat him down and plodded back
to the safety of my castle.

While I was there and inventory-shuffling, I had my second apply-katana
moment of the game.  I put a wand of cancellation into a bag of
holding.  I was so *sure* I was putting it in the sack, but my fingers
just did it by reflex. One magical explosion later I was severely down
on material. Lost my favorite loot-carrying tool. Lost my shimmering
golden +4 mummy wrapping. Lost my awesome blessed tinning kit. *Gulp*
+7 Mjollnir was in there too.

But I still had +7 Excalibur and my +7 katana, which I'd kind of been
preferring anyway since that Mojo-tossing incident earlier.  Still had
a sackful of rings and wands, food, holy water... could've been MUCH
worse.

Other noteworthy pre-Rodney things:
- After noticing that they were the only thing left that made me freak
out and run away, genocided R.
- After sack-swapping for a while at burdened, found a BoH in
Orcus-town shops.
- Juiblex, Orcus, Baalzebub, all those other named demons are minor
annoyances. I think I over-prepared at the castle.
- Vlad is a wuss, but I like his place.
- Tamed a couple of umber hulks, Chewie and Crunch, and let them play
around in the mazes of Gehennom.  (I was really glad for this later)
- While fooling around with a nurse, AC1, the Orb warned me of a red 2
coming around the corner.  I can take that bare-handed and naked, no
problem right? Before I knew what to do I got green-slimed. Did an
uncontrolled Orb and came up somewhere safe to pray. *whew*.  (Isn't
everybody proud of me for not genociding P?)
- Intentionally acquired teleportitis.  Handy but a pain to have to
wear a =oTC all the time, so I started attacking and eating peaceful
tengu.  No TC intrinsic.
- Clever me again. I decided to cursed-genocide tengus.  But--and this
is the "clever" part--so I didn't get an alignment penalty for killing
peacefuls, I put on an HoOA.
- AC shot up by 9 and it didn't go back down when I took the helmet
off. ugggggggh.  (still no TC intrinsic)
- I looted the chest named piggy bank...
- unwielded Excal, took off my GDSM, and let a vampire bite me
repeatedly.  Dropped from lev25 to lev20, then Orb/hiked to minetown
and the only remaining living priest.  Stupidly leveled up by killing
something annoying on the way, and only got to naked AC3 instead of
naked AC1, but when fully equipped, the difference between -38 and -40
is not too much to worry about.
- I found a magic lamp and used it as a light source, also as a
possible emergency backup wish.  I had already screwed up every chance
at voluntarily making this hard (stupidity may yet make it hard, but is
not voluntary), so for my personal "voluntary conduct" I decided that
if possible I'd ascend without burning that last wish.

After I went all the way down and found the VS, I got nervous.  This
could seriously be "it."  Glad to have made it this far, but not
wanting to fail after all this... I *really* over-prepared.

- made some SDSM (the "hard way," another first)
- cobbled together fully 3 AK's (+5CoMR/+4SDSM/=oL,
"oR/+5robe/+4GDSM/=oL, +0CoMR/+1EMM/+2SoR/LevBoots).
- put the SDSM/CoMR combo on (kept a backup +0 robe for non-battle
spellcasting) so I could wear an amulet of Life Saving.
- There were not enough candles in Mine Town.  But by poly-zapping
unihorns (trying for a magic marker) I got all the candles I needed (No
marker though)
- I cursed 3 !oGL just-in-case and blessed like 20 !oFH, which was
about the only potion left that I hadn't turned into holy water or
smoky potions.
- Made lotsa holy water.  Blessed 2 extra luckstones,(named TURN ME
OVER PLEASE and THANKS THATS MUCH BETTER). Blessed a stack of ?oRC,
bagged and stashed them all over.
- put my second-best kit up on the first level, along with some holy
water, potions, food, wands, oil, booze, ?oGD, blessed +3Snickersnee
(sac gift), and anything else I didn't need for the fight at hand and
thought may come in handy in the endgame.
- After dropping the stuff on dlvl 1 I went down all the steps dropping
blessed K-rations.
- I left the third-best Kit and Sting (random pickup) in a chest on a
burnt E-square by the stairs at the castle level. Couldn't think of
anything that could happen so bad that I'd need those, but I had it and
I'd make it easy, because who knows what may come.
- Tamed a couple of Angels.  Let them pick through my
backup-backup-backup equipment, zapped them invisible and fast.

Once I was pretty thoroughly convinced that there was no way I could
possibly screw this up, I gave the Wizard of Yendor a housecall.  Lost
an angel in the zoo, rubber-chickened a purple worm, killed the WoY in
a melee attack--it only took 3 or four chop-chops from b+7Excalibur and
b+7 katana, and aside from boiling some potions, and cursing a few
things, he didn't much hurt me back. Ate his corpse.  I'm a cannibal,
but still no TC intrinsic. Orb'ed to the VS level ... well 2 levels up
(whoops).  Peformed the invocation.  Went on down.  snuck through the
graveyard.  Is this whole room surrounded by Towers of Flame???  Ok,
fortunately I only had one potion and scroll out at the time. Jump in
